# Why this file exists — measured on this repo, not inherited.
#
# setuptools' legacy sdist default matches only `tests/test*.py`. It therefore
# omitted `tests/conftest.py` and `tests/__init__.py`. conftest.py defines the
# fixtures four of the five shipped test modules depend on, so the suite that
# shipped inside the sdist could not run: installing the published 0.2.1 sdist
# and running its own tests/ gave **58 passed, 38 errors** — every error a
# fixture lookup failing at setup. Only tests/test_fdic.py survived.
#
# This reproduces ONLY from a clean checkout. A local `python -m build` in a
# working tree that already has `cdfi_benchmark.egg-info/` reuses the stale
# SOURCES.txt, which lists conftest.py, and produces a CORRECT sdist. Since
# `*.egg-info/` is gitignored, CI never has that seed — so the artifact CI ships
# is broken while the one a maintainer builds by hand looks fine. Verified: the
# file list of the 0.2.1 sdist on PyPI is identical to a fresh-clone build.
#
# FIFTH instance of this defect in the portfolio: sbic-tracker, oz-tracker,
# cdfi-fund-tracker and nmtc-mapper all hit it first. This repo is the first of
# a four-repo sweep that fixes the remaining ones together; hmda-analyzer,
# cdfi-data and nmtc-application-builder are instances six, seven and eight,
# and each names its own number. (Do not copy this ordinal forward unchanged --
# four files all claiming to be the fifth is how the count stops being
# evidence.) The fix was written four times and propagated nowhere, so this
# change is paired with a `test-sdist` job
# in release.yml that unpacks the built tarball and runs ITS suite. The
# MANIFEST.in is only what makes that job pass; the job is what stops this from
# silently regressing. Packaging that is never installed from is packaging that
# is never verified.
recursive-include tests *.py

include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include pyproject.toml
include setup.py

# examples/ is intentionally NOT shipped — the demo notebook is a repo artifact,
# not part of the distributed package.
prune examples

global-exclude *.pyc
global-exclude __pycache__/*
